\vspace{-1ex}
\section{Conclusion}
This letter investigated a dual FA-assisted UAV network for MU-MIMO downlink communications. We first introduced a general channel model to capture the phase-related features between mobile UAVs and users. To maximize the average achievable rate, we proposed an AO algorithm which iteratively optimizes the UAV trajectory, transmit/receive FA port selection, and beamforming for decomposition of the non-convex problems. Numerical results verified that the proposed algorithm achieves significant throughput gains over FPA-based and existing FA-based baselines. Moving forward, our research will extend to multi-UAV cooperation, imperfect channel information, and hardware-constrained FA designs.
